meta {
  name: Create Share Link
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads/share-links
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "Referrals from Dave at First National"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // Runtime-only vars for the public-intake requests. Never setEnvVar — the
  // token is a working credential for an unauthenticated write endpoint.
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("shareLinkId", res.getBody().id);
    bru.setVar("shareLinkToken", res.getBody().token);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("token is 43 URL-safe characters", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().token).to.match(/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}$/);
  });

  test("url embeds the token and no internal identifiers", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.url).to.contain("/f/lead/" + body.token);
    expect(body.url).to.not.contain("producerId");
  });

  test("starts active with a zero submission count", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().isActive).to.equal(true);
    expect(res.getBody().submissionCount).to.equal(0);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /leads/share-links — generate a public intake link (PAC-37)

  Mints an opaque token a producer can share. Anyone holding the resulting URL
  can submit a lead, and it lands **pre-assigned to the producer who minted it**.

  - **Module:** `leads`
  - **Permission:** `leads:write`
  - **Data scope:** `own` — a link is **always** minted for the caller.

  ## Why a token, not a producer id in a query param
  The original proposal was `?producerId=<ObjectId>`. That fails three ways: an
  ObjectId is guessable and swappable, so anyone could reroute leads to a
  different producer; it leaks internal identifiers; and a leaked link could
  never be revoked. The indirection fixes all three, and lets us count
  submissions per link.

  ## Body
  | field | type   | required | notes                                                    |
  |-------|--------|----------|----------------------------------------------------------|
  | label | string | no       | max 120 chars. **Display only** — a producer's own note so they can tell links apart. It never reaches the created lead. |

  There is deliberately **no `producerId` field**. That is how "a producer cannot
  generate a link on behalf of another producer" is satisfied — by construction,
  with no scope-branching to get wrong. An injected `producerId` is silently
  dropped by the validator. Delegation belongs with PAC-53.

  This story also pins no lead source, partner attribution or branding on a link;
  those are PAC-53. The collection is shaped so they can be added as optional
  fields without reshaping it.

  ## Response `201`
  ```json
  {
    "id": "665f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293",
    "token": "8Kj2mQ7xR4tY9wZ1aB3cD5eF6gH8iJ0kL2mN4oP6qRs",
    "url": "http://localhost:5173/f/lead/8Kj2mQ7xR4tY9wZ1aB3cD5eF6gH8iJ0kL2mN4oP6qRs",
    "label": "Referrals from Dave at First National",
    "isActive": true,
    "submissionCount": 0,
    "lastSubmissionAt": null,
    "createdAt": "2026-08-03T10:14:22.000Z",
    "revokedAt": null
  }
  ```
  `url` is built from the `PUBLIC_FORM_BASE_URL` environment variable (defaults
  to `http://localhost:5173`).

  > The token is stored and returned in plaintext because this endpoint and the
  > list endpoint must hand it back so a producer can re-copy their URL — which
  > rules out hashing it. With no expiry in this story, a leaked link stays live
  > until revoked; **revocation is the containment mechanism.**

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — `label` longer than 120 characters.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `leads` module disabled, or missing `leads:write`.
}
